What is it?
-----------

BDay V1.2 [16-Feb-1998] PostCard Ware. Add this ARexx program to
your sys.welcome and Greet your users with a birthday gift and/or
gift :) I have seen several (well 2 anway) Birthday programs like
this for CNet. Both are nice and work well, however, this one gives
you far more control over display and gifts than any of the others.
You can use an exteranl ansi screen should you not like the builtin
screen. You can give gifts of Byte credits, File credits, Game Points
and Extra online time or you can give any combination of these :) You
control what to give and in what amounts. On the users first call on
thier birthday, they are shown either the internal or external scrrens
and on each other call on their birthday, a nice birthday message will
greet them.

As always, Use at your own risk. It works great here but may bomb
elsewhere.

Installation:
-------------

Read History.Doc for past version notes.


1. Unarch the program :) Lets hope this part is already done.
2. Move the BDay directory to Doors. You may move it elsewhere but if
   you do, be sure and edit the 'path' config.
3. Add this line to your sys.welcome.
   {#0Doors:BDay/BDay.rexx}
   ^
   Remember that the { is a CTRL-Q character
4. Save :)

Thats it! Simple.

Operation:
----------

Simple :) Just add it as an arexx pfile in your sys.welcome, config,
and it will do all of the rest.

Sysop Program Options:
----------------------

PATH='doors:BDay/' /* Path to your external BDay screen   */
AW1=0              /* AW1=0; Byte Credits (0=No/1=Yes)    */
AW2=0              /* AW2=0; File Credits (0=No/1=Yes)    */
AW3=0              /* AW3=0; Game Credits (0=No/1=Yes)    */
AW4=0              /* AW4=0; Time Credits (0=No/1=Yes)    */
AM1=250000         /* AM1=Amount of Award (Byte)          */
AM2=5              /* AM2=Amount of Award (File)          */
AM3=10             /* AM3=Amount of Award (Game)          */
AM4=30             /* AM4=Amount of Award (Time)          */
UE=0               /* UE=Use External Screen (0=No/1=Yes) */
EG=0               /* EG=External Gift (Text)(0=No/1=Yes) */

The numbers shown above are the defaults set in the program.

